&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering at Monzo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have 500+ engineers across Monzo who design and build our in-house banking platform. We have big ambitions for the future, and technology plays a big role in creating a bank our customers want, so engineers at Monzo collaborate across disciplines to solve interesting challenges throughout the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These range from the products our customers use everyday to underlying infrastructure, security, payments and finance, customer operations, financial crime, and data, to name just a few areas. As a bank, there is scope for impact across a huge number of opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We contribute to &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/monzo&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open source software&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; as much as possible. Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/technology&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;blog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;is a good place to learn even more about what we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Interns&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer intern at Monzo, you’ll be matched with a team where you’ll spend the summer working on a real project for our customers. We’ll pair you with a mentor who will support you to design and ship a solution to solve a real problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll have the opportunity to work alongside engineers to learn more about software engineering and the types of challenges engineers at Monzo solve on a day-to-day basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll spend your internship:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing, testing and shipping code that supports new features for our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing code for your colleagues, to pick up any improvements and learn from your peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with product managers, designers and data analysts on your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning about new technologies, engineering practices and what a full-time software engineering role looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively seeking out feedback to improve and accelerate your learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be using:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We rely heavily on the following tools and technologies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://golang.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to write our application code (there’s an excellent interactive Go tutorial &lt;a href=&quot;https://tour.golang.org/welcome/1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://cassandra.apache.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cassandra&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for most persistent data storage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://kafka.apache.org/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kafka&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for our asynchronous message queue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://kubernetes.io/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.docker.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Docker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; to schedule and run our services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://aws.amazon.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for most of our production infrastructure and&lt;a href=&quot;https://cloud.google.com/&quot;&gt; &lt;strong&gt;GCP&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for most of our data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://facebook.github.io/react/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for our public web apps and internal tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Kotlin for our Android app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Swift for our iOS app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 We’d love to hear from you if…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are completing a degree in Computer Science or another technical field with exposure to programming and are graduating in 2028&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy learning about new technologies and have a passion for problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
